  <section class="bg-[#F8F8F5] py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm p-8 md:p-12 prose prose-lg max-w-none">

        <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          You pull the door shut, hear the click, and your stomach drops. Locked out of my house, in Dover, DE. It happens to everybody eventually. Usually it's the groceries, or the dog waiting by the window, or a Tuesday night when you just wanted to get inside. Most of these end with the door opened and the lock fine. What decides that is the first ten minutes. Check the easy things, leave the door frame alone, and call a mobile locksmith before you grab a tool.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#A61E22] bg-[#F8F8F5] px-6 py-4 my-8 not-italic">
          <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-2">Key Takeaways</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-700 space-y-1 mb-0">
            <li>Give the easy checks five minutes before you call anyone.</li>
            <li>Forcing the door or breaking a window turns a small problem into a damaged door.</li>
            <li>Ask any locksmith for a business name and an ETA before they head your way.</li>
            <li>If the key was lost instead of locked inside, rekey the lock once you're in.</li>
          </ul>
        </blockquote>
        <h2 id="what-counts-as-a-house-lockout" class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-10 mb-4">What Counts as a House Lockout?</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Any time your normal key won't get you through your own door, that's a lockout. Sometimes the key is sitting on the kitchen counter. Sometimes it's gone for good. Sometimes it snapped off in the lock, or it slides in and just won't turn.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Which one you've got decides who you call, so spend half a minute figuring it out.
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6 not-prose">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm border border-gray-200">
            <thead class="bg-[#1A1F22] text-white">
